"""Render the completed proposal experiment as a self-contained HTML report."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
root=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];out=root/'output/proposal_knn'
r=json.loads((out/'results.json').read_text())
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>MPPCA-space neighbor experiment</title><style>body{font:16px system-ui;background:#111827;color:#e7edf8;max-width:1100px;margin:30px auto;padding:0 20px}p{color:#b7c7da;line-height:1.6}select{padding:10px;background:#26374d;color:white}canvas{width:100%;background:#172437}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:14px}td,th{padding:10px;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #34465c}.scroll{overflow:auto}a{color:#93c8ff}.note{font-size:14px}</style><h1>Does kNN in MPPCA space improve sampling?</h1><p>100,000 Bluesky posts · original vectors · 32 proposals per decision · 60 paired trials × 60 decision steps · 64 possible user locations</p><label>Shared feedback model <select id="world"><option value="chord">Embedding chord distance</option><option value="fermat_graph">Density-weighted graph distance</option></select></label><h2>Locating simulated users</h2><p class="note">Success means the posterior on the true location first reaches 50% within the budget. Intervals are 95% bootstrap intervals conditional on this fixed dataset, proposal bank and feedback model.</p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Proposal method</th><th>Success rate</th><th>Final true-location probability</th><th>Final MAP accuracy</th><th>Capped steps to threshold</th></tr></thead><tbody id="trials"></tbody></table></div><h2>Belief in the true location over time</h2><canvas id="curve" width="1000" height="340"></canvas><p id="legend"></p><h2>Same beliefs, same proposal budget</h2><p class="note">100 fixed synthetic posteriors. Each method chooses the most informative actual post after proposal-to-post retrieval. This isolates proposal quality from later feedback differences.</p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Best candidate information (bits)</th><th>Regret vs finite union oracle (bits)</th><th>Unique candidates / 32</th></tr></thead><tbody id="frozen"></tbody></table></div><h2>Retrieval diagnostics for the same proposals</h2><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Distance to retrieved post</th><th>Outside owner box before clipping</th><th>Distinct retrieved posts</th></tr></thead><tbody id="snaps"></tbody></table></div><p class="note">All MPPCA variants use the same synthetic proposals. Latent kNN searches all available posts in the generating component’s posterior latent coordinates. The top-5 variant draws one neighbor per proposal to preserve the 32-candidate budget. The full metric also penalizes off-subspace differences. Local actual posts remains a control, not a proposal-snapping method.</p><p class="note">Proposal banks contain 64 samples per hypothesis region and are reused. Feedback scales are frozen to the previous experiment. The original-space and actual-post baselines reproduce their previous scores. Repeated posts are excluded after presentation; a draw with no unseen candidates consumes a decision step without feedback. Capped steps assign 61 to failures, not an estimated uncensored stopping time. Actual-post baselines need post IDs; all methods use exact vectors for this offline retrieval/evaluation.</p><p class="note">Models were previously fitted on this corpus. Target post IDs are excluded from retrieval, but their vectors influenced training; this is a transductive simulation, not unseen-user validation. A single fixed hidden interest and a correctly specified response likelihood favor localization. No human preference claim follows.</p><p><a href="results.json">Complete results</a> · <a href="trials.csv">Trial records</a> · <a href="../../docs/Proposal_KNN.md">Protocol and interpretation</a></p><script>const D=__DATA__;const $=id=>document.getElementById(id),names={mppca:'Original-space 1NN',latent_1nn:'MPPCA latent 1NN',latent_5nn:'MPPCA latent top-5 sample',ppca_metric_1nn:'PPCA full-metric 1NN',local_latent_5nn:'Within-region latent top-5',local_original_1nn:'Within-region original 1NN',local_real_posts:'Local actual posts'},colors=['#7bb6fc','#e8bb6e','#62dbb0','#ef94c2','#b6a6fa','#ee806c','#d5e177'];function interval(s,percent=false){let k=percent?100:1;return (s.mean*k).toFixed(percent?1:3)+(percent?'%':'')+' ['+s.ci95.map(v=>(v*k).toFixed(percent?1:3)).join(', ')+']'}function render(){const world=$('world').value;$('trials').innerHTML=D.sequential.filter(r=>r.world===world).map(r=>'<tr><td>'+names[r.method]+'</td><td>'+interval(r.success_rate,true)+'</td><td>'+interval(r.final_true_mass)+'</td><td>'+interval(r.map_accuracy,true)+'</td><td>'+interval(r.capped_steps)+'</td></tr>').join('');$('frozen').innerHTML=Object.entries(D.frozen[world]).map(([m,s])=>'<tr><td>'+names[m]+'</td><td>'+interval(s.best_ig_bits)+'</td><td>'+interval(s.oracle_regret_bits)+'</td><td>'+s.mean_unique_candidates.toFixed(1)+'</td></tr>').join('');$('snaps').innerHTML=Object.entries(D.diagnostics).map(([m,s])=>'<tr><td>'+names[m]+'</td><td>'+s.mean_snap_distance.toFixed(3)+'</td><td>'+(100*s.outside_before_clipping).toFixed(1)+'%</td><td>'+s.unique_posts+'</td></tr>').join('');const c=$('curve'),ctx=c.getContext('2d');ctx.clearRect(0,0,c.width,c.height);ctx.font='14px system-ui';for(let t=0;t<=1;t+=.25){let y=300-t*270;ctx.strokeStyle='#34465c';ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(50,y);ctx.lineTo(980,y);ctx.stroke();ctx.fillStyle='#bacade';ctx.fillText(t.toFixed(2),5,y+5)}Object.keys(names).forEach((m,k)=>{ctx.strokeStyle=colors[k];ctx.lineWidth=2;ctx.beginPath();D.curves[world+'_'+m].forEach((v,i)=>{const x=50+i/59*930,y=300-v*270;i?ctx.lineTo(x,y):ctx.moveTo(x,y)});ctx.stroke()});ctx.fillStyle='#bacade';ctx.fillText('1',50,325);ctx.fillText('Decision steps →',420,325);ctx.fillText('60',960,325);$('legend').innerHTML=Object.keys(names).map((m,k)=>'<span style="color:'+colors[k]+'">● '+names[m]+'</span>').join(' &nbsp; ')}$('world').onchange=render;render();</script></html>'''
(out/'demo.html').write_text(html.replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(r).replace('<','\\u003c')))
